d} :question/id #uuid "7667b041-07ed-5199-9efb-833c8da623ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-332148" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n${\\cos }^{4}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-2{\\cos }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}){\\sin }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})+{\\sin }^{4}⁡({67.5}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\cos }^{4}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-2{\\cos }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}){\\sin }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})+{\\sin }^{4}⁡({67.5}^{∘}) & ={({\\cos }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-{\\sin }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}))}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{\\cos }^{2}⁡x-{\\sin }^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={67.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\cos }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-{\\sin }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {67.5}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({\\cos }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-{\\sin }^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}))}^{2} & ={\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d11a4f8-ffee-5767-9368-4c4c6f3d7aec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d11a4f8-ffee-5767-9368-4c4c6f3d7aec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302940} :answer-field/id #uuid "51165ca4-38a6-5ad0-bb61-4d9760434384" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304298}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f3454171-a1b3-502e-bdda-985c2af86469" :question/math-academy-id "q-332150" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {cos}^{4}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)-2{cos}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right){sin}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)+{sin}^{4}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{4}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)-2{cos}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right){sin}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)+{sin}^{4}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right) & ={\\left({cos}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)-{sin}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{\\cos }^{2}⁡x-{\\sin }^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)-{sin}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\cos \\,\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\cos \\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\left({cos}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)-{sin}^{2}\\,\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right)}^{2} & ={\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d347f734-6ca7-5952-bea8-22d7f06f35a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d347f734-6ca7-5952-bea8-22d7f06f35a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303767} :answer-field/id #uuid "f93642d3-ae42-5979-8df4-3afa14978559" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304747}] :question/difficulty {:db/ide